  parts: 87   score: 93/100  (prev 88)
  critique: The render is genuinely strong: TOP cleanly resolves eight blue BRAM banks, the copper multiplier column, the symmetric add/sub comb, the Barrett reduction spine and the offset exploded cluster, while FRONT/SIDE confirm everything rests on the ground line with the read/twiddle/return buses on standoffs and the heatsink correctly lifted on its riser. The visual axes are at their ceiling. The two soft spots versus the rubric were (a) recognizability — a bare placed-and-routed board reads as a generic PCB because the most iconic accelerator-card cue, a host edge connector, was absent and the data path had no origin; and (b) proportional grounding cited too few dimensional facts. The deepest unresolved failure is still buildability: the headline conflict-free bank/offset equations, the modulus q, psi/omega and the FSM table remain reproduction defaults, honestly flagged but not the paper's verified values, so a competent engineer cannot yet rebuild it bit-exactly.
  + Added a PCIe x16 gold-finger host edge connector (host_edge) protruding from the -X board edge plus a host DMA/PCIe controller block (host_phy), completing the data path host -> PHY -> input FIFO -> BRAM banks and BRAM -> output FIFO -> PHY -> host, so the board now reads unmistakably as an NTT coprocessor accelerator card.
  + Wired input_fifo and output_fifo to host_phy, added host_edge/host_phy to pcb_substrate connections, and reordered assembly_instructions to seat the host interface first.
  + Densified the exploded heatsink from 7 to 10 fins at 0.3 pitch (heatsink_fin_0..9) with a fin-count/pitch note on the baseplate, improving recognizability, structural decomposition and geometric fidelity.
  + Replaced the two least-numeric facts (Radix support, Publication — both already implied by the machine_name and sources[]) with dimensional/numeric ones: Pipeline latency (9 cycles/lane = mult 3 + add/sub 1 + Barrett 4 + reg 1) and Board footprint (14 x 9, banks/lanes at 1.1 pitch); annotated bank pitch on the parallel-BU fact.
  · gap: Transcribe the paper's actual Sec. III conflict-free bank-index/offset functions (its headline result) into crossbar_network and addr_gen_unit and reconcile with o(i)=i>>3 — this is the single largest remaining buildability gain (~2-3 pts) and is the reason this pass is not converged.
  · gap: Replace q=12289 (reproduction default) with the paper's benchmark modulus and recompute mu (currently 21843 at k=28) and N_inv (currently 8857 = 1024^-1 mod 12289).
  · gap: Pin a concrete primitive 2048-th root psi mod q and store its power table in twiddle_rom.spec for bit-exactness; psi/omega are currently given only by their defining congruences.
  · gap: Verify schedule_controller.fsm transition table and the stage/block loop bounds against the paper's scheduling figure and confirm they yield the 33% mult / 20% add-sub counts.
  · gap: Confirm pipeline latencies (mult 3 / add-sub 1 / Barrett 4 / reg 1 = 9) against the paper's reported cycle counts and clock for the 1024-pt 8-BU radix-4 core.
  · gap: Visual axes are at ceiling — do not add further decorative parts; future gains must come from source-grounded numbers, not geometry.
